
1. OVERVIEW
A custom message encryption and decryption system inspired by
classical cryptography.

2. CHARACTER CONVERSION
- Convert each character into its corresponding Unicode value.
- Process the numeric values.
- Convert the resulting values back into characters.

3. ENCRYPTION MECHANISM
- Receive the original message.
- Convert characters into Unicode values.
- Add the generated numeric key to each value.
- Convert the resulting values back into characters.

4. DECRYPTION MECHANISM
- Receive the encrypted message.
- Convert characters into Unicode values.
- Subtract the same numeric key.
- Convert the resulting values back into characters.

5. KEY GENERATION MECHANISM
- Receive a numeric string.
- Traverse the string according to the custom pairing rule.
- Determine whether to use addition or subtraction.
- Calculate the resulting numeric key.

6. MESSAGE EXCHANGE
- The sender encrypts the original message.
- The sender shares the ciphertext and numeric code.
- The receiver enters the ciphertext and numeric code.
- The application generates the key and decrypts the message.

7. TESTING
- English characters.
- Vietnamese characters.
- Special symbols.
- Unicode characters outside the Basic Multilingual Plane.
- Empty input and invalid numeric input.

8. TECHNICAL NOTES
- JavaScript implementation.
- Unicode code point handling.
- Encryption and decryption consistency.
- Known limitations.